From: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 09:05:06 -0700
Subject: GPU: Clamp max_texture_image_units to 13 on PowerVR GPUs

Limit max_texture_image_units to 13 on PowerVR GPUs via workaround
max_texture_image_units_13 across ContextGroup, GLCapabilities,
and the Passthrough command decoder.

Bug: 548085797
Change-Id: I38766bde1399d6f40f32840439f415ee7fda8e77
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8297925
Auto-Submit: Zhenyao Mo <zmo@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Kenneth Russell <kbr@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1687286}

Electron adaptation notes (42-x-y):
- gpu_driver_bug_list.json: the branch already carries later
  workaround entries (ids 492/493 via merges), so the new id 491
  entry is appended after them instead of after id 490.
- webgl2_conformance_expectations.txt: context drift only; both the
  branch's and the upstream expectation lines are kept.

